+  <section class="section discussion-section"><div class="wrap discussion-layout"><div><p class="section-number">06 / <span data-zh="技术讨论">Technical discussion</span></p><h2 data-zh="值得追问的设计选择。">The decisions<br>worth discussing.</h2><p data-zh="这项工作的价值，在于选择合适的动作语义，并让数据、模型和底盘接口遵守同一份约定。">The engineering value is in choosing an appropriate action meaning—and making the dataset, policy, and base interface agree on it.</p></div><div class="discussion-list">
+      <details><summary><span data-zh="为什么使用车体系相对位姿？">Why use body-relative poses?</span><span class="detail-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p data-zh="同一个局部行为可以在不同 ODOM 起点与朝向下共享相同动作标签。先相减再旋转到当前车体系，可减少标签对全局坐标选择的依赖。状态若仍包含绝对 ODOM，则不能据此声称整个策略严格具有平移、旋转不变性。">The same local behavior can share an action label across different ODOM origins and headings. Subtraction followed by rotation into the base frame reduces the label's dependence on global coordinates. If state still contains absolute ODOM, this alone does not make the entire policy strictly invariant.</p></details>
+      <details><summary><span data-zh="为什么整段 chunk 使用同一个参考？">Why freeze the reference for the whole chunk?</span><span class="detail-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p data-zh="每个未来目标都可直接解码，无需累加前面的预测。这避免了逐帧增量组合造成的额外误差链，但不会消除里程计漂移、模型预测误差或控制跟踪误差。新一轮推理才更新参考位姿。">Each future target can be decoded directly without integrating previous predictions. This avoids an additional chain of incremental decoding errors, while odometry drift, prediction errors, and tracking errors remain. The reference updates at the next inference cycle.</p></details>
+      <details><summary><span data-zh="这个方法来源于哪篇论文？">Which paper is this based on?</span><span class="detail-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p data-zh="整体是基于 GR00T 的底盘工程适配。动作表示与 UMI 的 relative trajectory 思想一致：整段未来末端目标相对同一当前位姿；UMI 使用 SE(3)，这里处理平面底盘的 SE(2)。这属于方法对应关系，不声称是开发时的直接灵感来源。SE(2) 坐标变换本身是机器人学基础。">The project is an engineering adaptation of GR00T for a mobile base. Its representation aligns with UMI's relative-trajectory idea: future end-effector targets share one current reference. UMI uses SE(3); this project uses planar SE(2). This is a methodological connection, not a claim about the project's historical inspiration. The coordinate transform itself is standard robotics.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://umi-gripper.github.io/umi.pdf#page=6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UMI · PD2.1 & Fig. 6 ↗</a></details>
+      <details><summary><span data-zh="为什么不直接采用 Mobile ALOHA 的动作？">How does this differ from Mobile ALOHA?</span><span class="detail-plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p data-zh="Mobile ALOHA 为底盘和双臂联合学习提供了相关先例，但它的底盘动作是线速度与角速度。这里的数据和控制接口以 ODOM 目标位姿为基础，所以采用三维相对位姿表示；两者不是同一套动作协议。">Mobile ALOHA is relevant precedent for learning base and arm actions together, but its base actions are linear and angular velocities. This project's data and control interface use ODOM target poses, motivating a three-dimensional relative-pose representation. The action contracts are different.</p></details>
